   "text": "I read the molecule as a macrocyclic peptide and wrote the SMILES by following the ring from the lysine residue around to the diaminobutyric acid residue.\n\n- **Lysine residue:** the \u03b1-carbon carries a wedged 4-aminobutyl chain, and the C-terminal carbonyl is bonded to an N-methyl nitrogen.\n- **N-methyl tryptophan residue:** the \u03b1-carbon carries a wedged CH2 to an indol-3-yl group, and its carbonyl links through NH\u2013CH2 to the fluorinated benzene ring.\n- **Fluorinated benzene ring:** going round the ring, the CH2-bearing carbon sits between the S-bearing carbon and the carbon bearing the pyridone. F is on the carbon next to the S-bearing carbon, and two CH carbons complete the ring.\n- **Pyridone and pyridine:** the pyridone is attached at its 4-position, with N1 carrying an (E)-CH=CH\u2013COOH group. A thioether S links the benzene ring to C2 of the pyridine, and the pyridine C3 carries CH2\u2013NH.\n- **Diaminobutyric acid residue:** that NH is the \u03b1-nitrogen of a 2,4-diaminobutyric acid unit with a wedged CH2CH2NH2 side chain, and its carbonyl closes the ring onto the lysine NH.\n\n**Stereochemistry:** from the wedge directions, all three \u03b1-carbons come out as S (L-configuration). The SMILES patterns match standard L-amino-acid SMILES. The enamide-type double bond is drawn trans, so I wrote it as E.\n\nSMILES: NCCCC[C@H]1C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2c[nH]c3ccccc23)C(=O)NCc4c(c(F)ccc4-c5ccn(/C=C/C(=O)O)c(=O)c5)Sc6ncccc6CN[C@@H](CCN)C(=O)N1"
